Recent versions of neovim now automatically attempt to set the value of termguicolors based on the capabilities of the terminal emulator. This works really well, but there is one thing that I'm struggling with in mini.basics.
I would like to have mini.basics set the value of options.extra_ui to false if termguicolors is also false (and vice versa if it is true).
I tried to do this by evaluating the value of termguicolors in the config like so:
local basics_config = function()
	local opts = {
		options = {
			basic = true,
