The callable form of textobject specification [takes same arguments](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/04f8d6e0acd5a52d01ec1c392e3947135dbfd8ef/doc/mini-ai.txt#L249-L250) as [`MiniAi.find_textobject()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/04f8d6e0acd5a52d01ec1c392e3947135dbfd8ef/doc/mini-ai.txt#L532-L546). For this particular case using only the first one `ai_type` should allow returning two different regions based on it.

Coincidentally, there is a direct solution to this particular problem [in `MiniExtra.gen_ai_spec.line()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/04f8d6e0acd5a52d01ec1c392e3947135dbfd8ef/lua/mini/extra.lua#L198-L209). So either copy paste the code or use it directly in 'mini.ai'. With something like this:

```lua
require('mini.extra').setup()
require('mini.ai').setup({
  custom_textobjects = {
    L = MiniExtra.gen_ai_spec.line(),
  },
})
```

