reply_data.body:
Welcome!

> 1. How do I show the relative path (or just the file name) in the statusline instead of the absolute path?

Where exactly do you want to show only file name? If as on screenshot, then it is configured in `config.content.inactive`. It can be set to the function which uses `'%t'` string to show file "tail" instead of [currently used `'%F'` to show full path](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b07157c51e52a1b004ec7959f9618e9bc24686d3/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L635). So something like this would be enough:

```lua
require('mini.statusline').setup({
  content = {
    inactive = function() return '%#MiniStatuslineInactive#%t%=' end,
  },
})
```

If it is in the active window, then it is a bit more complicated and involves setting `config.content.active` to custom function. The default content is [present in the help file](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b07157c51e52a1b004ec7959f9618e9bc24686d3/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L86-L106) and it shows full path for windows wider than 140 columns and only filename for narrower ones. Adjusting that involves copying that function to your config/'init.lua' and adjusting it to fit your need.

> 2\. I'm using NeoTree as a file explorer. How can I disable the statusline when NeoTree is open and prevent it from showing anything in the statusline?

All 'mini.nvim' modules can be disabled per buffer by setting dedicated buffer-local variable. For ['mini.statusline' it is `vim.b.ministatusline_disable`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b07157c51e52a1b004ec7959f9618e9bc24686d3/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L70-L76). Your case fits the ["Disable for a certain filetype"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/b07157c51e52a1b004ec7959f9618e9bc24686d3/doc/mini.txt#L339-L341) disabling recipe.

